<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><title>Building QA from scratch | Alice Paggi</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/style.css"></head><body class="case-page"><main><section class="case-hero"><div class="container"><a class="case-back" href="../index.html#work">← Back to selected work</a><div class="case-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">CASE STUDY 01 · QA OWNERSHIP</p><img class="case-logo case-logo-generali" src="../assets/generali-logo-clean.png" alt="Generali"><h1 class="case-title">Building QA<br>from scratch.</h1><p class="case-subtitle">From a single tester to a scalable QA process across Web and Mobile.</p><p class="case-copy">At Generali, I was the only Test Engineer for an extended period. I took ownership of the QA process from the ground up, then helped scale the team as the product and international scope grew.</p><div class="case-meta"><div><small>Role</small><strong>Test Engineer</strong></div><div><small>Platforms</small><strong>Web · iOS · Android</strong></div><div><small>Markets</small><strong>Italy + international</strong></div><div><small>Ownership</small><strong>End-to-end QA</strong></div></div></div><div class="case-visual case-visual-generali"><img src="../assets/generali-agent-hub.png" alt="Generali Agent Hub across web and mobile devices"></div></div></div></section></main><script src="../js/main.js"></script></body></html>